13. Thus, to satisfy the definition of proprietary food, a material:
1. must be an article of food;
2. must not be one standardised under the Food Safety and Standards (Food Products Standards and Food Additives) Regulations, 2011;
3. must not be one notified by the Central Government as novel foods, foods for special dietary uses, foods for special medical purposes, functional foods,
nutraceuticals, health supplements or such other food articles and;
4. should not be any deviation in quality parameters of a standardised food.
